# Frontend UI (leaderboard system)

When editing public-facing layout or leaderboard UI, follow:

- [frontend/docs/design.md](frontend/docs/design.md) — colors, type, layout, podium rules
- [frontend/docs/components.md](frontend/docs/components.md) — component names and scope

## Rules

- Use Tailwind tokens (`background`, `on-surface`, `primary`, `font-headline`, etc.), not ad-hoc hex unless defining a one-off gradient from design.md.
- Do not use DaisyUI `table`, `stat`, or light-theme `alert-*` on the homepage leaderboard (`RankingsComponent` and `leaderboard/*`).
- Keep branding: Dutch Lankan Shuttle Masters + existing logo — not COURTCLAN.
- Points column shows real `rankScore`; do not fake mock-scale numbers.
- Reuse `LeaderboardRow`, `FormBars`, `TrendIndicator` instead of duplicating row markup.

Admin pages may still use DaisyUI until restyled; new public chrome (nav/footer) should match the dark system.
